Working state|git status --short --branch|Summarizes branch and file changes.|Check for local work before switching or rewriting history.|The two status columns describe index and working-tree changes; ?? means untracked.|## feature...origin/feature ; M app.js|Read-only; does not show ignored files by default.
Unstaged diff|git diff|Compares working-tree content with the index.|Review edits not yet staged.|Minus lines are removed and plus lines added relative to the index; staged-only changes are absent.|diff --git a/app.js b/app.js|Read-only; output may contain secrets introduced locally.
Staged diff|git diff --staged|Compares the index with HEAD.|Review exactly what a normal commit would include.|Only staged changes appear; later unstaged edits may differ.|--- a/file ; +++ b/file|Read-only; inspect before committing.
Whitespace validation|git diff --check|Checks the selected diff for whitespace errors and conflict-marker problems.|Catch accidental formatting damage before review.|Output names files and lines with issues; no output usually means no detected issue.|file:12: trailing whitespace|Read-only; this is not a syntax or semantic test.
Fetch remote state|git fetch origin|Downloads objects and updates origin remote-tracking references.|Inspect upstream changes without integrating them into the current branch.|Updated reference ranges show what changed; the working tree stays unchanged.|abc123..def456 main -> origin/main|Changes local remote-tracking refs and contacts the remote; does not merge.
History graph|git log --graph --oneline --decorate -20|Shows a compact recent commit graph with reference names.|Understand branching, merges and the current base.|Stars are commits; connecting lines show parent relationships; labels identify refs.|* abc123 (HEAD -> feature) Fix validation|Read-only; the graph is limited to the selected history and count.
Commit details|git show --stat HEAD|Displays the current commit summary and file-change statistics.|Review the scope of the latest commit.|The stat counts changed lines by file; use a full diff for actual content.|3 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)|Read-only; statistics do not establish correctness.
Branch tracking|git branch -vv|Lists local branches with tips and upstream information.|Find a branch tracking the wrong remote or lacking an upstream.|Brackets show upstream and ahead/behind relative to last fetched state.|* main abc123 [origin/main] ...|Read-only; fetch first when current remote state matters.
Ignore diagnosis|git check-ignore -v PATH|Explains which ignore pattern matches a path.|Find why a generated or source file does not appear as expected.|Output identifies rule file, line number and pattern.|.gitignore:12:dist/ dist/app.js|Read-only; replace PATH and remember tracked files are not untracked ignore candidates.
Local recovery history|git reflog --date=iso -10|Shows recent local reference movements.|Locate a commit lost after reset or rebase.|Each entry includes a reachable historical tip and the operation that moved it.|HEAD@{...}: rebase (finish): ...|Read-only; entries expire and do not guarantee recovery of uncommitted changes.
Changed filenames|git diff --name-status origin/main...HEAD|Lists changes introduced since the merge base with origin/main.|Review branch scope relative to its base.|A, M and D indicate added, modified and deleted paths; three dots use the merge base.|M app.js|Read-only; ensure origin/main is freshly fetched and is the intended comparison branch.
Release tags|git tag --list 'v*' --sort=-version:refname|Lists version-like tags in version-aware descending order.|Inspect available release references.|Names are tags, not proof that an artifact exists or was verified.|v2.1.0 ; v2.0.0|Read-only; verify tag identity and release artifact separately.
Repository location|git rev-parse --show-toplevel|Prints the root of the current working tree.|Confirm which repository a script or terminal is operating in.|The output is an absolute path; an error means the current location is not inside a recognized working tree.|/work/project|Read-only; verify this before running commands that change index or history.
Configured remotes|git remote -v|Lists remote names and fetch/push URLs.|Verify where changes will be retrieved from or published to.|Fetch and push URLs may differ; a familiar remote name does not prove its destination.|origin https://github.com/OWNER/REPO.git (fetch)|Read-only; URLs can contain sensitive credentials in poorly configured repositories.
Create a working branch|git switch -c feature/clear-prompts|Creates a branch at the current commit and switches to it.|Isolate a new change before committing.|The switch confirmation names the new branch; existing uncommitted edits may come along if compatible.|Switched to a new branch 'feature/clear-prompts'|Mutates local branch/worktree selection; inspect status and intended starting commit first.
Stage selected hunks|git add -p -- PATH|Interactively stages chosen changes from a file.|Separate unrelated edits into reviewable commits.|Each hunk prompt asks whether to stage the shown diff; review git diff --staged afterward.|Stage this hunk [y,n,q,a,d,s,e,?]?|Mutates the index, not the remote; only stage understood changes.
Unstage without discarding|git restore --staged -- PATH|Restores an index entry from HEAD while retaining working-tree edits.|Remove an accidental file change from the next commit.|Usually silent on success; git status and git diff show the retained unstaged work.|No output on success|Mutates the index. Do not omit --staged if the intention is to keep working-tree changes.
Create a local commit|git commit -m 'Clarify practice question context'|Creates a commit from the staged snapshot.|Record one reviewed change with a useful explanation.|The summary gives a new commit ID and file statistics; unstaged edits remain outside it.|[feature/clear-prompts SHA] Clarify practice question context|Mutates local history and can run repository hooks. Review staged content and test results first.
Inspect a complete commit|git show --format=fuller COMMIT|Displays commit metadata and its patch.|Understand exactly what a candidate release or recovery commit changed.|Author and Commit dates can differ; the patch shows the change relative to parent context.|commit SHA ... diff --git ...|Read-only; replace COMMIT with a verified reference.
Find line history|git blame -L 20,40 -- PATH|Shows the last recorded change attribution for selected lines.|Find relevant history before modifying unfamiliar behavior.|Each line includes a commit ID, author metadata and line content; attribution is not proof of fault or original design intent.|SHA (Author DATE 20) code|Read-only; follow the referenced commits to understand surrounding changes.
Fast-forward integration|git merge --ff-only origin/main|Updates the current branch only if the integration can fast-forward.|Avoid silently creating a merge commit when synchronizing a linear branch.|Fast-forward output means no merge commit was needed; failure means histories diverged and need an explicit decision.|Updating OLD..NEW Fast-forward|Mutates the local branch and files; preserve uncommitted work and confirm the current branch first.
Reverse a published change|git revert COMMIT|Creates a new change that reverses a selected commit.|Undo an approved bad change while preserving published history.|A new commit is created after any conflicts are resolved; external effects and database migrations are not automatically reversed.|[branch NEW_SHA] Revert ...|Mutates files/history; review dependent changes and special handling for merge commits before use.
Apply a selected fix|git cherry-pick COMMIT|Applies a commit's patch as a new commit on the current branch.|Backport an isolated verified fix.|The new commit usually has a different ID; conflict messages require semantic resolution, not blind marker removal.|[release NEW_SHA] Fix ...|Mutates branch and working tree; inspect prerequisites and run relevant tests.
Preserve temporary work|git stash push -u -m 'before investigation'|Stores tracked edits and untracked files, then cleans them from the working tree.|Temporarily set aside work before a local investigation.|The saved message identifies a local stash; ignored files are not included by -u.|Saved working directory and index state ...|Mutates local files; inspect the stash and avoid treating it as a remote backup.
Inspect a stash|git stash show -p stash@{0}|Displays the patch represented by a stash entry.|Check saved work before restoring it.|The diff shows changes in that stash; confirm the entry name because new stashes change numeric positions.|diff --git a/file b/file ...|Read-only; sensitive edits remain visible in the patch.
Start regression bisection|git bisect start BAD_COMMIT GOOD_COMMIT|Starts binary-search selection between known bad and good revisions.|Narrow a reproducible regression to its introducing commit.|Git checks out a candidate and reports remaining steps; mark each candidate good or bad after the same reliable test.|Bisecting: ... revisions left to test|Changes the checkout, usually to detached HEAD. Preserve edits first and use git bisect reset to finish.
Exit regression bisection|git bisect reset|Ends a bisect session and returns to the original checkout.|Restore normal development context after finding or abandoning a regression search.|The checkout summary identifies the restored branch/commit; any test-created edits still need inspection.|Previous HEAD position was ... Switched to branch ...|Mutates checkout state; inspect local changes before ending a session.
Separate working tree|git worktree add ../project-review -b review/changes origin/main|Creates another working tree with a new branch.|Review or implement independent work without disturbing the current checkout.|The destination contains its own working files while sharing repository objects.|Preparing worktree (new branch 'review/changes')|Writes a directory and creates a branch. Choose an unused destination and verify the base ref.
Annotated release tag|git tag -a v1.2.3 -m 'Release v1.2.3' COMMIT|Creates a local annotated tag for a verified commit.|Record release metadata before an authorized publication.|Usually silent; inspect with git show v1.2.3. This does not publish the tag or prove artifact provenance.|No output on success|Mutates local refs; confirm version, target commit and release policy before creating or pushing.
Compare release contents|git diff --stat BASE_COMMIT RELEASE_COMMIT|Summarizes file changes between two revisions.|Check the scope of a candidate release before reading detailed patches.|Each row shows a file and insertion/deletion counts; statistics alone cannot prove correctness.|src/app.js 12 ++++++------|Read-only; verify both reference identities and inspect substantive patches separately.
